 * Works from the inside out, repeatedly stripping the innermost tag until the
 * string stabilises. This neutralises interleaved delimiters — e.g. a `{% %}`
 * nested inside `{{ }}` (or vice versa) — that a single pass would leave behind
 * as an injectable expression. Unpaired delimiters (an opening `{{`/`{%` with no
 * matching close) never match and are left untouched.
